        "comments": "The assembly daSolCann1.hap1.1 is based on 42x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species is tetraploid (2n = 36). One haplotypic inversion was detected on Chromosome 1 from 7.39 to 9.24 Mbp..The HAP1 file is chromosome-level and contains the most complete set of chromosomes. The other 3 haplotypes are scaffold-level and are in HAP2 file.",
